# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# Playwright: installed deps and per-run artifacts (traces, screenshots)
node_modules/
test-results/
playwright-report/
# What start-stack.sh publishes about the stack it booted, for the
# multi-host tests that have to reach behind the API (see that script).
# Per-run and removed by its cleanup trap.
e2e/.stack-info.json
# Minted by Playwright's global auth setup and removed with the stack.
e2e/.auth/storage-state.json
# The browser suite's per-slot equivalents of both (e2e/stack-slots.ts).
e2e/.stacks/

# Leftover of the removed pinned test tmux build, which existing checkouts may
# still hold (a built tmux and its build tree). Nothing creates it any more and it
# is safe to delete; it stays ignored so that jj, which tracks new files on its
# own, never sweeps one into a commit.
.ci-tmux/

# Verified local tool binaries; release and CI jobs install into their temporary directory.
.ci-nextest/
.ci-cargo-deny/
# The pinned dx the deleted Dioxus UI was built with. Nothing installs it any more; it stays ignored so that jj never
# sweeps an old checkout's copy into a commit.
.ci-dx/

# Personal use-it-for-real dev-loop script; carries user-specific hostnames
# and stays out of the repo on purpose.
/scripts/laptop-dev.sh

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Delegation run directories (scode-agent-delegation): prompts, checkpoint
# files, and review reports private to the session that created them.
.agent-delegation/

# What the README hero capture's stack script publishes about the fleet it
# booted (e2e/readme-hero/start-stack.sh); per run, removed by its trap.
e2e/readme-hero/.stack-info.json
# The demo video's equivalent (e2e/readme-video.config.ts), same lifecycle.
e2e/readme-video/.stack-info.json
# The docs screenshots' equivalents (e2e/docs-shots.config.ts): the stack info and
# the staged fleet's ids, both per run.
e2e/docs-shots/.stack-info.json
e2e/docs-shots/.fleet.json
__pycache__/

# Astro build output and content-collection cache for the docs website;
# Vercel builds website/dist itself and nothing in the repo consumes it.
website/dist/
website/.astro/
# Docs screenshots captured locally by scripts/docs-screenshots.sh, shown by the
# preview and read by scripts/publish-docs-shots.sh; published images live off
# main (docs/docs-shots/SPEC.md).
website/public/docs-shots-local/
# The Release notes page, generated from CHANGELOG.md on every website build
# and preview start (website/scripts/release-notes.mjs).
website/src/content/docs/docs/release-notes.mdx
